@namespace TimeWarp.Architecture.Features.Applications
@inherits BaseComponent
@using Ai = Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.AI
@using TimeWarp.Architecture.Components
@using TimeWarp.Architecture.Services

@*
  Purpose: Ask panel. A person describes what they want and the in-app model runs a page catalog tool.

  Design: Docked in TimeWarpPage's FluentLayout aside (450px), not a modal and not a flex
  sibling of the layout. The top-bar "Ask {AssistantName}" button and the Ctrl-K Ask row both open it.
  The page reflows beside it; below 880px and when expanded the aside item covers the viewport.
  It renders the probe's state (task 293): only when the server answered "no key" does it show
  "AI not configured" and that environment's setup hint. Signed out (401) shows "Sign in to use
  Ask" and a button that closes the panel and goes to Login with the current page as the return
  path. Any other failure shows the status, title and detail and a Retry that runs the probe
  again. The probe itself re-runs on every sign-in and sign-out (AuthenticationStateListener).
  Tools are the palette's agent-visible commands, the current page's tools, navigate, site_map,
  and page_context, the same list WebMCP publishes, including the approval bit for the
  conversation's edit mode. Global actions, site_map and navigate work from any page, including
  Home: the instructions carry the menu's site map for this principal (task 300), so Ask answers
  about any permitted page, links it, and navigates there (with approval in Ask before editing). A page-bound action off its page
  returns a navigate offer and does not run. The route is PageAgentRoute, which
  this panel refreshes from the browser location on WebAssembly before it rebuilds. Tool arguments
  render as JSON. An empty argument dictionary is omitted: Razor would print its CLR type name,
  and page_context's schema is empty so that dictionary is {}. The tool result stays in the model
  transcript and is not copied into the reasoning block. The panel rebuilds the agent when
  the route, the edit mode, or the conversation generation changes. A route or edit-mode rebuild
  never runs while a turn is streaming or waiting on an approval card: it waits for the turn to
  go idle. New conversation (a generation change) rebuilds at once and abandons that turn. A build
  that finishes after the panel was disposed (navigation mid-build) frees what it created.
  The root carries data-built-mode, the edit mode of the agent actually built.
  The transcript is not a component field. Every agent gets the AskConversationThread for the
  current generation (AskConversationThreads, app-scoped), and the panel owns the AgentContext
  instead of ChatPage's AgentBoundary, so it can await AgentContext.RestoreAsync before the
  MessageList attaches. That restores both the rendered turns and the model history across Close,
  navigation (TimeWarpPage remounts), and rebuilds. New conversation bumps the generation and
  gets an empty thread. The markup mirrors ChatPage (sc-ai-chat-page body and footer).
  MessageInput stays the library component. Scoped CSS turns its flex row into a two-row
  grid: the textarea spans the full width and grows with field-sizing up to 10rem, and send
  sits on the footer row. Typing @ at the start of a word in the composer (not mid-word, as in
  an email address) opens AskReferencePicker (task 345): the
  site-wide resource types the person may list, then a search of the chosen type's list query;
  choosing an item inserts its @prefix:id token at the caret. The Tag button in the composer's
  lead slot (task 346) dispatches AskTagState.StartPick for the current route: pick mode
  highlights the app's marked elements (AskTagMark) and the chosen one becomes a chip
  (AskTagChips) above the composer. The agent's client is AskTagChatClient over the tool-invoking
  client, so the chips go out with the next message and then move to page_context.tags.
  The panel shows "Picking" from AskTagState.IsPicking, which turns on only once ask-tag.ts has
  armed the pick (task 351), and Tag stays disabled while a pick is arming or armed (IsPickPending).
  StartPick is not a tracked action, so it does not raise the app-wide busy signal. Closing the
  panel, disposing it, and any location change cancel pick mode; every request re-renders the
  instructions, so page_context.tags in them is current.
  Closing the panel also closes the reference picker.
  The empty state is AskStarterPrompts (task 348): the configured XAI:StarterPrompts cards, or the
  template defaults.
  Look (task 349, after the Cloudflare dashboard chat): a compact one-row header (avatar, assistant name,
  the conversation name, icon actions) over a hairline; a dotted canvas body; a centered empty
  state of CSS gradient orbs in the brand colors, a greeting, a tagline and the cards; and a
  footer pinned to the bottom with the notice, chips and a raised composer. The composer's lead slot
  holds Tag and AskEditModePill (task 355), the pill that shows and switches the edit mode, so the
  edit mode is set only once the agent is built. AskSettingsMenu (task 356), the sliders button that
  shows the conversation credential's status and links to Agent links, also renders in the lead
  slot: MessageInput's TrailingActions replaces the send button, so the composer grid places it in
  a trail area just left of send instead. Its tab stop therefore comes before the textarea.
  AskSendButton (task 357) is a leading action too: it draws the FluentUI arrow-up glyph over the
  library send button, which stays the send action, and swaps in a Stop button while an answer
  streams. This file's CSS gives the round button its muted (empty or in flight) and solid
  (sendable) states.
  The body fills the panel between header and footer and scrolls on its own. AskAnswerBar sits
  first in the footer, right under the latest answer: MessageList renders its ChildContent above
  the turns, so inside the list the bar would land at the top of the transcript. Every color is a
  --twe-* token, and the library's --sc-ai-* tokens are mapped onto them on the panel root, so the
  transcript follows the template theme.
  AskPrivacyBanner (task 347) sits in the footer, directly above the composer. The first
  render restores its local-storage dismissal before the agent (and so the footer) is built.
  It mints one short-lived credential for the signed-in principal when a conversation has none.
  The credential is an advisory client-side guardrail, not a security boundary: its scopes are a
  copy of every permission claim the principal holds now, a null credential means unbounded, and
  server [EndpointAuthorize] remains the boundary. When it has expired the header says so and
  points at New conversation. Outcomes of dispatched actions stay on NotificationState. Copy and
  @ insertion are presentational JS on child components.
  Identity (task 361): every label here is AgentSurfaceState.AssistantName (default Akili, admin-set
  on SiteSettings): the header title, the sign-in and error states, the greeting "Hi, I'm {name}",
  the conversation credential's label and the instructions' first line. The instructions read the
  name on every request, so a rename while an agent is built reaches the model at its next turn.
  The credential's label is fixed when it is issued: an open conversation keeps the name it began
  with until New conversation, while the header shows the current one. The avatar is the
  server-made Multiavatar for the name. The header shows it (alt is the name) in place of 349's
  gradient mark, which stays as the fallback until the identity loads; the empty state shows it
  in front of the orbs; and each assistant turn shows it through --twe-assistant-avatar, which
  ApplyAvatarAsync sets on the document root because the library renders the turns and inline
  styles are banned.
  Screenshot (task 303-001): the camera button in the lead slot dispatches
  ScreenshotState.CaptureForAsk, which draws the page body (the page behind this panel, since the
  panel lives in the layout aside) and attaches that capture in the same handler.
  AskScreenshotChip shows it as a removable thumbnail above the composer. The
  agent's client chain is AskTagChatClient over AskScreenshotChatClient over the tool-invoking
  client, so the next message carries the picture as image content and MarkAskSent clears it.
  Replies (task 380): a BlockRenderer for RichContentBlock keeps the library's message bubble
  markup and renders an assistant block's RawText through SafeMarkdown (CommonMark soft breaks,
  no images, http(s) links in a new tab). A user block (Role is User) stays plain text. The
  library re-renders the list on every streamed fragment, so the reply re-parses as it grows.
  An app-relative link dispatches RouteState.ChangeRoute (TWA0026) and leaves the panel open.
  Focus (task 381): MessageInput has no focus API, so focus goes through ask-ai.ts on the library
  textarea. OpenAskPanel raises AgentSurfaceState.ComposerFocusPending on every open path. The
  first render keeps the opener (CaptureOpener, which also claims the palette's focus return, so
  the Ctrl-K row's palette close never lands on top of the composer). The request is consumed in
  OnAfterRenderAsync once a render drew the built agent: the composer takes focus and the request
  clears. Signed out, not configured and error have no composer, so the request is dropped there
  and a later build does not pull focus. A navigation remount sees no request and does not
  refocus; an edit-mode or route rebuild does not either. While an approval card waits
  (AwaitingInput) nothing moves focus; the request waits for the turn to settle. A send (the
  conversation going Streaming) and the expand toggle each ask for the soft form once the turn is
  idle: the composer takes focus only if focus is in the panel or on nothing. Disposing a closed
  panel returns focus to the opener, or to the page main region when the opener is gone.
*@

@code {
  private const string AskPlaceholder =
    "Tell the app what you want. Type @ to reference a resource.";

  [Inject] private IServiceProvider ServiceProvider { get; set; } = null!;
  [Inject] private IActionCatalog ActionCatalog { get; set; } = null!;
  [Inject] private NavigationManager NavigationManager { get; set; } = null!;
  [Inject] private IJSRuntime JsRuntime { get; set; } = null!;
  [Inject] private PageAgentRoute PageAgentRoute { get; set; } = null!;
  [Inject] private IStore ScopedStore { get; set; } = null!;
  [Inject] private AskConversationThreads Threads { get; set; } = null!;

  private Ai.UIAgent? Agent;
  private Ai.AgentContext? Conversation;
  private AskConversationThread? Thread;
  private IDisposable? StatusSubscription;
  private FunctionInvokingChatClient? InvokingClient;
  private AskTagChatClient? TagClient;
  private CatalogAgentFunctions? Functions;
  private bool Building;
  private bool Disposed;
  private int DeclinedGeneration = -1;
  private string? BuiltPath;
  private AgentEditMode BuiltMode;
  private int BuiltGeneration = -1;
  private bool AvatarApplied;
  private string? AppliedAvatar;

  private string AssistantName => AgentSurfaceState.AssistantName;
  private string Greeting => $"Hi, I'm {AssistantName} \u2014 what can I help with?";

  private CatalogAgentReadiness Readiness => CatalogAgentAvailability.Readiness(AgentSurfaceState);
  private string SetupCommand => CatalogAgentAvailability.SetupCommand(AgentSurfaceState);
  private string? AdminHint => CatalogAgentAvailability.AdminHint(AgentSurfaceState);
  private string? KeyHint => CatalogAgentAvailability.KeyHint(AgentSurfaceState);
  private string ConversationTitle =>
    string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(AgentSurfaceState.ConversationDisplayName)
      ? "New conversation"
      : AgentSurfaceState.ConversationDisplayName;
  private string? Problem => CatalogAgentAvailability.Problem(AgentSurfaceState);

  private bool ConversationExpired =>
    AgentConversationAuthority.IsExpired(AgentSurfaceState.Conversation, DateTimeOffset.UtcNow);

  private bool TurnInProgress =>
    Conversation?.Status is Ai.ConversationStatus.Streaming or Ai.ConversationStatus.AwaitingInput;

  protected override void OnInitialized()
  {
    base.OnInitialized();
    NavigationManager.LocationChanged += OnLocationChanged;
  }

  // Pick mode belongs to the page it started on; CancelPick is a no-op when nothing is picking.
  private void OnLocationChanged(object? sender, LocationChangedEventArgs args)
  {
    if (!Disposed)
    {
      _ = InvokeAsync(() => AskTagState.CancelPick());
    }
  }

  protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
  {
    await base.OnAfterRenderAsync(firstRender);
    if (firstRender)
    {
      if (AgentSurfaceState.ComposerFocusPending)
      {
        await CaptureOpenerAsync();
      }

      await AgentSurfaceState.LoadPrivacyNoticeDismissal();
    }

    await ApplyAvatarAsync();

    PageAgentRoute.Observe(NavigationManager, JsRuntime);
    await IssueConversationAsync();
    Ai.UIAgent? previous = Agent;
    await EnsureAgentAsync();
    if (!ReferenceEquals(previous, Agent))
    {
      StateHasChanged();
    }

    await SettleComposerFocusAsync(previous);
  }

  // The composer is on screen only when the render that just ran drew the agent that is still built.
  private async Task SettleComposerFocusAsync(Ai.UIAgent? rendered)
  {
    bool composerShown = rendered is not null && ReferenceEquals(rendered, Agent) && Conversation is not null;
    if (AgentSurfaceState.ComposerFocusPending)
    {
      if (Readiness is CatalogAgentReadiness.NotConfigured or CatalogAgentReadiness.Unauthenticated or CatalogAgentReadiness.Error)
      {
        await AgentSurfaceState.ClearComposerFocus();
        return;
      }

      if (!composerShown || Conversation?.Status == Ai.ConversationStatus.AwaitingInput)
      {
        return;
      }

      SendFocusPending = false;
      ExpandFocusPending = false;
      await FocusComposerOnOpenAsync();
      await AgentSurfaceState.ClearComposerFocus();
      return;
    }

    if (composerShown && !TurnInProgress && (SendFocusPending || ExpandFocusPending))
    {
      SendFocusPending = false;
      ExpandFocusPending = false;
      await FocusComposerInPanelAsync();
    }
  }

  // Set when a turn starts streaming and when expand toggles; consumed once the turn is idle.
  private bool SendFocusPending;
  private bool ExpandFocusPending;

  [DirectComponentSideEffect("Keeps the element focused when the panel opened, to hand focus back on close; focus is DOM state.")]
  private Task CaptureOpenerAsync() => AskAiJsModule.CaptureOpenerAsync(JsRuntime);

  [DirectComponentSideEffect("Focuses the library composer textarea on open; MessageInput has no focus API and focus is DOM state.")]
  private Task FocusComposerOnOpenAsync() => AskAiJsModule.FocusComposerOnOpenAsync(JsRuntime);

  [DirectComponentSideEffect("Returns focus to the library composer after a send or expand when focus is still in the panel; focus is DOM state.")]
  private Task FocusComposerInPanelAsync() => AskAiJsModule.FocusComposerInPanelAsync(JsRuntime);

  [DirectComponentSideEffect("Returns focus to the panel's opener when the closed panel goes away; focus is DOM state.")]
  private void RestoreOpener() => _ = AskAiJsModule.RestoreOpenerAsync(JsRuntime);

  private string CurrentPath() => PageAgentRoute.PathOr(NavigationManager);

  [DirectComponentSideEffect("Sets the --twe-assistant-avatar CSS property the library-rendered assistant turns draw; presentational, and inline styles are banned.")]
  private async Task ApplyAvatarAsync()
  {
    string? avatar = AgentSurfaceState.AssistantAvatar;
    if (AvatarApplied && avatar == AppliedAvatar)
    {
      return;
    }

    AvatarApplied = true;
    AppliedAvatar = avatar;
    await AskAiJsModule.SetAssistantAvatarAsync(JsRuntime, avatar);
  }

  private async Task IssueConversationAsync()
  {
    if (AgentSurfaceState.Conversation is not null)
    {
      return;
    }

    if (DeclinedGeneration == AgentSurfaceState.ConversationGeneration)
    {
      return;
    }

    // Re-read on every issue. The panel does not cache an AuthenticationState.
#pragma warning disable BL0013
    AuthenticationState authentication = await AuthenticationStateProvider.GetAuthenticationStateAsync();
#pragma warning restore BL0013
    string? idText = authentication.User.FindFirst(ClaimTypes.NameIdentifier)?.Value;
    if (!Guid.TryParse(idText, out Guid principalId))
    {
      DeclinedGeneration = AgentSurfaceState.ConversationGeneration;
      return;
    }

    List<string> scopes = [];
    foreach (Claim claim in authentication.User.FindAll(PermissionIds.ClaimType))
    {
      if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(claim.Value))
      {
        scopes.Add(claim.Value);
      }
    }

    int minutes = AgentSurfaceState.CredentialLifetimeMinutes;
    TimeSpan lifetime = minutes > 0
      ? TimeSpan.FromMinutes(minutes)
      : AgentConversationCredentialIssuer.DefaultLifetime;
    AgentConversationCredential credential = AgentConversationCredentialIssuer.Issue
    (
      principalId,
      scopes,
      DateTimeOffset.UtcNow,
      lifetime,
      $"{AssistantName} conversation"
    );
    await AgentSurfaceState.SetConversation
    (
      credential.Id,
      credential.PrincipalId,
      scopes.ToArray(),
      credential.ExpiresAt,
      credential.DisplayName
    );
  }

  private async Task EnsureAgentAsync()
  {
    if (Readiness != CatalogAgentReadiness.Configured)
    {
      if (Agent is not null)
      {
        ReleaseAgent();
      }

      return;
    }

    string path = CurrentPath();
    AgentEditMode mode = AgentSurfaceState.EditMode;
    int generation = AgentSurfaceState.ConversationGeneration;
    if (Agent is not null && BuiltPath == path && BuiltMode == mode && BuiltGeneration == generation)
    {
      return;
    }

    // A rebuild disposes the AgentContext, which cancels the stream and orphans an approval card.
    // Wait for the turn to finish; the status callback re-renders and this runs again. New
    // conversation (a generation change) abandons the turn on purpose, so it does not wait.
    if (Building || (TurnInProgress && BuiltGeneration == generation))
    {
      return;
    }

    IChatClient? chatClient = ServiceProvider.GetService<IChatClient>();
    if (chatClient is null)
    {
      return;
    }

    Building = true;
    try
    {
      // Re-read on every rebuild. The panel does not cache an AuthenticationState.
#pragma warning disable BL0013
      AuthenticationState authentication = await AuthenticationStateProvider.GetAuthenticationStateAsync();
#pragma warning restore BL0013
      IReadOnlyList<CatalogAgentTool> selected = await CatalogAgentToolSet.SelectAsync
      (
        authentication.User,
        AuthorizationService,
        ActionCatalog.Entries,
        path,
        mode,
        CancellationToken.None
      );
      string siteMap = AgentSiteMap.Summary
      (
        await AgentSiteMap.DestinationsAsync(authentication.User, AuthorizationService, path),
        AgentAskInstructions.SiteMapCap
      );
      if (Disposed)
      {
        return;
      }

      ReleaseAgent();
      Functions = CatalogAgentFunctions.Create(selected);
      List<string> toolNames = [];
      foreach (CatalogAgentTool tool in selected)
      {
        toolNames.Add(tool.Name);
      }

      toolNames.Add(PageAgentContext.ToolName);
      // Rebuilt on every request (AskTagChatClient), so page_context.tags names the tags sent so far
      // and the first line names the assistant's current name, even after a rename mid-conversation.
      string RenderInstructions()
      {
        string assistantName = ScopedStore.GetState<AgentSurfaceState>().AssistantName;
        return AgentAskInstructions.For
        (
          assistantName,
          siteMap,
          PageAgentContext.Describe
          (
            ScopedStore,
            path,
            toolNames,
            liveSurfaceJson: null,
            AgentAskInstructions.ContextCapFor(assistantName, siteMap)
          )
        );
      }
      InvokingClient = CatalogAgentSession.CreateInvokingClient(chatClient, ServiceProvider);
      AskScreenshotChatClient screenshotClient = new
      (
        InvokingClient,
        () => ScreenshotState.AskAttachedFor(AgentSurfaceState.ConversationGeneration),
        id => InvokeAsync(() => ScreenshotState.MarkAskSent(id))
      );
      TagClient = new AskTagChatClient
      (
        screenshotClient,
        () => AskTagState.AttachedFor(AgentSurfaceState.ConversationGeneration),
        ids => InvokeAsync(() => AskTagState.MarkSent(ids)),
        RenderInstructions
      );
      AskConversationThread thread = Threads.For(generation);
      Ai.UIAgent agent = new
      (
        TagClient,
        options =>
        {
          options.ChatOptions = new ChatOptions
          {
            Tools = [.. Functions.Tools],
            Instructions = RenderInstructions(),
          };
          options.Thread = thread;
        }
      );
      Ai.AgentContext conversation = new(agent);
      // Restore before MessageList attaches: it reads Turns once, when its AgentContext changes.
      await conversation.RestoreAsync();
      if (Disposed)
      {
        // Dispose already released the fields; free what this build created.
        conversation.Dispose();
        agent.Dispose();
        ReleaseAgent();
        return;
      }

      Agent = agent;
      Conversation = conversation;
      Thread = thread;
      StatusSubscription = conversation.RegisterOnStatusChanged(OnStatusChanged);
      BuiltPath = path;
      BuiltMode = mode;
      BuiltGeneration = generation;
    }
    finally
    {
      Building = false;
    }
  }

  private static bool IsUserTurn(Ai.RichContentBlock block) => block.Role == Microsoft.Extensions.AI.ChatRole.User;

  private async Task OpenAppLinkAsync(string url) => await NoSubRouteState.ChangeRoute(newRoute: url);

  private async Task SignInAsync()
  {
    string returnPath = "/" + NavigationManager.ToBaseRelativePath(NavigationManager.Uri);
    await AgentSurfaceState.CloseAskPanel();
    await NoSubRouteState.ChangeRoute(newRoute: TimeWarp.Architecture.Features.Identity.LoginPage.GetLoginUrl(returnPath));
  }

  private Task RetryAsync() => AgentSurfaceState.LoadChatConfiguration();

  private void OnStatusChanged(Ai.ConversationStatus status)
  {
    if (!Disposed && status == Ai.ConversationStatus.Streaming)
    {
      SendFocusPending = true;
    }

    if (!Disposed && status is Ai.ConversationStatus.Idle or Ai.ConversationStatus.Error)
    {
      // A rebuild may have been deferred while the turn ran.
      _ = InvokeAsync(StateHasChanged);
    }
  }

  private void ReleaseAgent()
  {
    StatusSubscription?.Dispose();
    StatusSubscription = null;
    Conversation?.Dispose();
    Conversation = null;
    Thread = null;
    Agent?.Dispose();
    Agent = null;
    // TagClient owns the screenshot client, which owns InvokingClient (DelegatingChatClient
    // disposes its inner client).
    TagClient?.Dispose();
    TagClient = null;
    InvokingClient = null;
    Functions?.Dispose();
    Functions = null;
  }

  private string? RecordedApproval(Ai.FunctionApprovalBlock approval)
  {
    bool? answer = Thread?.ApprovalAnswer(approval.ApprovalRequest.RequestId);
    return answer switch
    {
      true => nameof(Ai.ApprovalStatus.Approved),
      false => nameof(Ai.ApprovalStatus.Rejected),
      null => null,
    };
  }

  [DirectComponentSideEffect("Reads the library textarea's caret to open the @ picker only when @ starts a word; the caret is DOM state, and opening is still the Open action.")]
  private async Task OnComposerKeyDownAsync(KeyboardEventArgs args)
  {
    if (args.Key != "@" || AskReferenceState.IsOpen)
    {
      return;
    }

    if (await AskAiJsModule.AtStartsWordAsync(JsRuntime))
    {
      await AskReferenceState.Open();
    }
  }

  private Task TagAsync() => AskTagState.StartPick(CurrentPath());

  private bool Capturing;

  private async Task CaptureAsync()
  {
    Capturing = true;
    try
    {
      await ScreenshotState.CaptureForAsk();
    }
    finally
    {
      Capturing = false;
    }
  }

  private bool Picking => AskTagState.IsPicking;

  private async Task CloseAsync()
  {
    await AskTagState.CancelPick();
    await AskReferenceState.Close();
    await AgentSurfaceState.CloseAskPanel();
  }

  private Task ExpandAsync()
  {
    ExpandFocusPending = true;
    return AgentSurfaceState.ToggleAskExpand();
  }

  private Task NewConversationAsync()
  {
    EditModeFocusPending = false;
    return AgentSurfaceState.NewConversation();
  }

  // The pill that chose a mode is replaced by the rebuild; its successor takes focus once. A turn in
  // progress defers the rebuild and the menu has already returned focus to the same pill, so nothing
  // waits: a later rebuild must not pull focus from wherever the person went.
  private bool EditModeFocusPending;

  private void EditModeChose() => EditModeFocusPending = !TurnInProgress;

  private void EditModeFocusRestored() => EditModeFocusPending = false;

  private string ExpandLabel => AgentSurfaceState.IsPanelExpanded ? "Collapse" : "Expand";

  private Icon ExpandIcon => AgentSurfaceState.IsPanelExpanded
    ? new Icons.Regular.Size20.FullScreenMinimize()
    : new Icons.Regular.Size20.FullScreenMaximize();

  public override void Dispose()
  {
    Disposed = true;
    NavigationManager.LocationChanged -= OnLocationChanged;
    if (AskTagState.IsPickPending)
    {
      _ = AskTagState.CancelPick();
    }

    ReleaseAgent();
    if (!AgentSurfaceState.IsPanelOpen)
    {
      RestoreOpener();
    }

    base.Dispose();
  }
}

<div class="twe-agent-ask" data-qa="AgentAsk" data-built-mode="@(Agent is null ? null : BuiltMode.ToString())">
  <header class="twe-agent-ask__header">
    <div class="twe-agent-ask__heading">
      @if (AgentSurfaceState.AssistantAvatar is { } avatar)
      {
        <img class="twe-agent-ask__avatar" src="@avatar" alt="@AssistantName" width="24" height="24" data-qa="AskAvatar" />
      }
      else
      {
        <span class="twe-agent-ask__mark" aria-hidden="true">
          <FluentIcon Value="@(new Icons.Filled.Size16.Sparkle())" Color="Color.Custom" CustomColor="var(--twe-on-primary)" />
        </span>
      }
      <div class="twe-agent-ask__titles">
        <h2 class="twe-agent-ask__title" data-qa="AskTitle">@AssistantName</h2>
        <p class="twe-agent-ask__conversation" data-qa="AskConversationTitle">@ConversationTitle</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="twe-agent-ask__header-actions">
      <FluentButton Appearance="ButtonAppearance.Subtle"
                    IconOnly="true"
                    IconStart="@(new Icons.Regular.Size20.ChatAdd())"
                    Title="New conversation"
                    Tooltip="New conversation"
                    aria-label="New conversation"
                    data-qa="AskNewConversation"
                    OnClick="NewConversationAsync" />
      <FluentButton Appearance="ButtonAppearance.Subtle"
                    IconOnly="true"
                    IconStart="@ExpandIcon"
                    Title="@ExpandLabel"
                    Tooltip="@ExpandLabel"
                    aria-label="@ExpandLabel"
                    data-qa="AskExpand"
                    OnClick="ExpandAsync" />
      <FluentButton Appearance="ButtonAppearance.Subtle"
                    IconOnly="true"
                    IconStart="@(new Icons.Regular.Size20.Dismiss())"
                    Title="Close"
                    Tooltip="Close"
                    aria-label="Close"
                    data-qa="AgentAskClose"
                    OnClick="CloseAsync" />
    </div>
  </header>
  <div class="twe-agent-ask__status" role="status">
    @if (ConversationExpired)
    {
      <p class="twe-agent-ask__expired" data-qa="AskConversationExpired">This conversation has expired, so page actions are refused. Choose New to start another.</p>
    }
  </div>

  @if (Readiness == CatalogAgentReadiness.NotConfigured)
  {
    <div class="twe-agent-ask__state">
      <p class="twe-agent-ask__state-title" data-qa="AgentAskNotConfigured">AI not configured</p>
      <p class="twe-agent-ask__state-text">Set the xAI key this way, then reload:</p>
      <pre class="twe-agent-ask__setup" data-qa="AgentAskSetupCommand">@SetupCommand</pre>
      @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(KeyHint))
      {
        <p class="twe-agent-ask__state-text" data-qa="AgentAskKeyHint">@KeyHint</p>
      }
      @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(AdminHint))
      {
        <p class="twe-agent-ask__state-text" data-qa="AgentAskAdminHint">@AdminHint</p>
      }
    </div>
  }
  else if (Readiness == CatalogAgentReadiness.Unauthenticated)
  {
    <div class="twe-agent-ask__state">
      <p class="twe-agent-ask__state-title" data-qa="AgentAskSignIn">Sign in to use @AssistantName</p>
      <div class="twe-agent-ask__actions">
        <FluentButton Appearance="ButtonAppearance.Primary" data-qa="AgentAskSignInButton" OnClick="SignInAsync">Sign in</FluentButton>
      </div>
    </div>
  }
  else if (Readiness == CatalogAgentReadiness.Error)
  {
    <div class="twe-agent-ask__state">
      <p class="twe-agent-ask__state-title" data-qa="AgentAskError">@AssistantName could not load its configuration</p>
      <pre class="twe-agent-ask__setup" data-qa="AgentAskErrorDetail">@Problem</pre>
      <div class="twe-agent-ask__actions">
        <FluentButton Appearance="ButtonAppearance.Outline" data-qa="AgentAskRetry" OnClick="RetryAsync">Retry</FluentButton>
      </div>
    </div>
  }
  else if (Agent is null || Conversation is null)
  {
    <div class="twe-agent-ask__state">
      <p class="twe-agent-ask__state-text" data-qa="AgentAskStarting">Starting @(AssistantName)…</p>
    </div>
  }
  else
  {
    @if (AskReferenceState.IsOpen)
    {
      <AskReferencePicker />
    }
    @* Mirrors ChatPage, with the panel's own AgentContext so the restored turns render. *@
    <div class="sc-ai-root sc-ai-chat-page" @key="Conversation">
      <CascadingValue Value="Conversation" IsFixed="true">
        <div class="sc-ai-chat-page__body">
          <Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.AI.MessageList>
            <ChildContent>
              <AskStatusLine />
              <Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.AI.BlockRenderer TBlock="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.AI.RichContentBlock" Context="text">
                <div class="sc-ai-message sc-ai-message--@(IsUserTurn(text) ? "user" : "assistant")">
                  <div class="sc-ai-message__bubble">
                    <div class="@(text.LifecycleState == Ai.BlockLifecycleState.Active ? "sc-ai-message__content sc-ai-message__content--streaming" : "sc-ai-message__content")">
                      @if (IsUserTurn(text))
                      {
                        @text.RawText
                      }
                      else
                      {
                        <SafeMarkdown Markdown="@text.RawText" DataQa="AskReplyMarkdown" OnAppLinkClick="OpenAppLinkAsync" ExternalLinksInNewTab="true" SoftBreaksAsSpaces="true" />
                      }
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.AI.BlockRenderer>
              <Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.AI.BlockRenderer TBlock="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.AI.FunctionInvocationContentBlock" Context="call">
                <details class="twe-agent-ask__reasoning" data-qa="AskReasoning">
                  <summary>See reasoning</summary>
                  <p>@call.ToolName</p>
                  @if (AgentArgumentText.Format(call.Arguments) is { } arguments)
                  {
                    <pre data-qa="AskReasoningArguments">@arguments</pre>
                  }
                </details>
              </Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.AI.BlockRenderer>
              <Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.AI.BlockRenderer TBlock="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.AI.FunctionApprovalBlock" Context="approval">
                <div class="twe-agent-ask__approval" data-qa="AgentApproval">
                  <p>Allow <strong>@approval.ToolName</strong>?</p>
                  @if (AgentArgumentText.Format(approval.Arguments) is { } approvalArguments)
                  {
                    <pre data-qa="AgentApprovalArguments">@approvalArguments</pre>
                  }
                  @if (RecordedApproval(approval) is { } recorded)
                  {
                    <p data-qa="AgentApprovalStatus">@recorded</p>
                  }
                  else if (approval.Status == Ai.ApprovalStatus.Pending)
                  {
                    <FluentButton Appearance="ButtonAppearance.Primary" data-qa="AgentApprove" OnClick="() => approval.Approve()">Approve</FluentButton>
                    <FluentButton Appearance="ButtonAppearance.Outline" data-qa="AgentReject" OnClick="@(() => approval.Reject("Declined."))">Reject</FluentButton>
                  }
                  else
                  {
                    <p data-qa="AgentApprovalStatus">@approval.Status</p>
                  }
                </div>
              </Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.AI.BlockRenderer>
            </ChildContent>
            <EmptyContent>
              <div class="twe-agent-ask__welcome">
                <div class="twe-agent-ask__hero">
                  <span class="twe-agent-ask__orb twe-agent-ask__orb--back" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                  <span class="twe-agent-ask__orb twe-agent-ask__orb--side" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                  <span class="twe-agent-ask__orb twe-agent-ask__orb--front" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                  @if (AgentSurfaceState.AssistantAvatar is { } heroAvatar)
                  {
                    <img class="twe-agent-ask__hero-avatar" src="@heroAvatar" alt="@AssistantName" width="56" height="56" data-qa="AskEmptyAvatar" />
                  }
                </div>
                <p class="twe-agent-ask__greeting" data-qa="AskGreeting">@Greeting</p>
                <p class="twe-agent-ask__tagline">Ask about this page, or tell the app what to do.</p>
                <AskStarterPrompts />
              </div>
            </EmptyContent>
          </Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.AI.MessageList>
        </div>
        <div class="sc-ai-chat-page__footer">
          <AskAnswerBar SupportUrl="@AgentSurfaceState.SupportUrl" />
          <AskPrivacyBanner />
          <AskTagChips />
          <AskScreenshotChip />
          <div class="sc-ai-chat-page__input-container" @onkeydown="OnComposerKeyDownAsync">
            <Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.AI.MessageInput Placeholder="@AskPlaceholder">
              <LeadingActions>
                <div class="twe-agent-ask__lead">
                  <FluentButton Appearance="ButtonAppearance.Outline"
                                Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                IconStart="@(new Icons.Regular.Size16.Tag())"
                                Title="Tag an element on the page"
                                Tooltip="Tag an element on the page"
                                aria-pressed="@(Picking ? "true" : "false")"
                                Disabled="AskTagState.IsPickPending"
                                data-qa="AskTag"
                                OnClick="TagAsync">Tag</FluentButton>
                  <FluentButton Appearance="ButtonAppearance.Outline"
                                Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                IconOnly="true"
                                IconStart="@(new Icons.Regular.Size16.Camera())"
                                Title="Attach a screenshot of the page"
                                Tooltip="Attach a screenshot of the page"
                                aria-label="Attach a screenshot of the page"
                                Disabled="Capturing"
                                data-qa="AskCapture"
                                OnClick="CaptureAsync" />
                  <AskEditModePill RestoreFocus="EditModeFocusPending"
                                   Chose="EditModeChose"
                                   FocusRestored="EditModeFocusRestored" />
                </div>
                @* TrailingActions would replace send; the grid moves this to the trail area. *@
                <div class="twe-agent-ask__trail">
                  <AskSettingsMenu />
                </div>
                @* The arrow-up glyph over the library send button, and Stop while an answer streams. *@
                <AskSendButton />
              </LeadingActions>
            </Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.AI.MessageInput>
          </div>
        </div>
      </CascadingValue>
    </div>
  }
</div>
